# Line endings.
#
# This repo had no attribute file, so it accumulated a mix: files written by Windows tooling
# arrived as CRLF while files written by the build arrived as LF. That stayed invisible until a
# scripted edit read a file with universal newlines and wrote it back, which silently converted
# two large files from CRLF to LF and buried ~960 lines of pure line-ending churn inside a commit
# whose real content was ten lines. Declaring the policy here means git normalises on the way in,
# so the working tree, the index and every clone agree and that cannot happen again.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Rasters, fonts and documents must never be line-ending rewritten.
*.webp  binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary

# Generated output. It is committed so the live site can be diffed, but it is produced by
# build.js and must not be hand-edited.
dist/** -text
